# Checks for `verify-deployed.sh`. INSTANCE-OWNED — the mechanism is the same across
# the estate, the checks are not. This file is seeded, never overwritten by a sync.
#
#   <name>  <persona-id>  <method>  <path>  <expect>
#
# `expect` is `non-empty` or `status:<code>`.
#
# The template ships no real checks: an instance's routes and personas are its own.
# `verify-deployed.sh --list` over an empty file correctly reports zero, which is the
# honest answer and not a pass.
#
# Example, from the instance that motivated this (biffo-fleet#167). A known-enrolled
# learner must still receive a NON-EMPTY list; a `200 []` means the tenant GUC did not
# bind and is a REVERT signal, because the route degrades silently rather than 500ing:
#
#   enrollments-nonempty  unit-staff  GET  /api/v1/lms/my/enrollments  non-empty
#
# Pick the persona deliberately. `unit-staff` is correct there only because the dev
# seed gives it a real enrolment; an admin persona would return empty for an entirely
# innocent reason and the check would read as a REVERT signal when nothing is wrong.
